{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3816","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3816","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3816\",\"parent_revision\":\"902380457cafc8119bd4eb369e7f2bbc1590b77e7e29e959b518b74c952d852f\",\"root_revision\":\"902380457cafc8119bd4eb369e7f2bbc1590b77e7e29e959b518b74c952d852f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nReplace the release playbook's repeated consumer-local base includes with self-contained GitLab CI/CD components using typed `spec:inputs`. Keep workflow admission, stage order, project builds, policy, and immutable component pins in the consumer root; use predefined GitLab variables for project and pipeline identity.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Five reusable component contracts cover semantic-release versioning, python-semantic-release versioning, release notes, Generic Package publication, and GitLab Release creation.\\n- Components contain no global workflow, stages, default, or top-level variables and do not depend on a copied shared base.\\n- A consumer composition owns orchestration and includes exactly one version adapter.\\n- Guidance explains dedicated component-project layout, immutable production pins, same-project SHA testing, credential boundaries, and consumer-owned builds.\\n- Tests validate executable structure and observable contracts rather than exact prose.\\n- Plugin validation and repository hooks pass.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e88a5d7ba69f27bf994734255fba1f6cac1d2a01924b93d8655982c6d368e0a7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCENlg\"}"}